export const CHINESE_SCORING = "## 2. 乙部 scoring (official)\n\n### 2.1 Criteria and maximum marks\n\n| Criterion | Max | What is assessed (verbatim, [SEM25] slides 42–43) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 內容 | 40 | 立意、內容是否合乎寫作要求；豐富、深刻。取材是否恰當；能彰顯立意。闡述是否合理、飽滿。 |\n| 表達 | 30 | 用詞是否精確、豐富（主）。文句是否簡潔流暢（主）。表達手法是否純熟靈活（輔）。 |\n| 結構 | 20 | 段落區分是否明晰。起承轉合是否自然。輕重詳略是否恰當。 |\n| 標點字體 | 10 | 字體為主，標點為輔。標點使用在於準確和靈活，不在於數量多少。 |\n| 錯別字 | 3 | 0–1個：3分；2–4個：2分；5–7個：1分；8個或以上：0分。**重錯不計**（a repeated error counts once）。 |\n| **Total** | **103** | 按各評分項目，就文章整體評分。 |\n\n### 2.2 品第 scale (the same for 內容, 表達, 結構 and 標點字體) [SEM25] slide 41\n\n| 品 | 品第 → points out of 10 |\n|---|---|\n| 上品 | 上上 10 · 上中 9 · 上下 8 |\n| 中品 | 中上 7 · 中中(上) 6 · 中中(下) 5 · 中下 4 |\n| 下品 | 下上 3 · 下中 2 · 下下 1 |\n| — | 極差劣／空白 0 |\n\n**Estimate:** the 10-point grade is multiplied by **×4 / ×3 / ×2 / ×1** for 內容 / 表達 / 結構 / 標點字體 to reach 40 / 30 / 20 / 10. HKEAA states the multiplier explicitly only for 甲部 內容 (「倍大為30分」); the ones here are worked out from the maximum marks.\n\n### 2.3 Caps (official, [SEM25] slide 44)\n- **Off-topic (離題):** 內容 ≤ 下上 · 表達 and 結構 ≤ 中上 · 標點字體 can still be 上上.\n- **Short essays** (character count includes punctuation), cap on 內容: 550–649 → 上上 · 450–549 → 中上 · 300–449 → 中中(下) · under 300 → 下上.\n  - This is as printed. The slide heading says 「不足650字」, yet 550–649 is still allowed 上上, so in practice the first real cap starts below 550. Possibly a slide error; see open issues.\n- Memorised \"model essays\" (背誦), where detected, are not marked for that portion [HB25].\n\n### 2.4 錯別字 and 繁體／簡體 (official, [SEM25] slide 45, [QA22] Q2, [QA25] Q1)\n- 「繁體字或簡化字均可接受。簡化字以中國政府2013年所頒布之《通用規範漢字表》為據。」\n- HKEAA says traditional and simplified may be mixed, even within the same sentence (「同一句句字同時採用繁體字和簡體字」).\n\n| 計作錯別字 (counted as wrong) | 不計作錯別字 (not counted) |\n|---|---|\n| 繁簡同體 (one character blending traditional and simplified parts) | 一個詞語中，一個簡體字，一個繁體字 |\n| 缺部件或增部件 (a missing or extra component) | 字體潦草 (scrawled handwriting, which is judged under 標點字體 instead) |\n| 「空格」造成詞意不連貫 (a gap that breaks the word) | 重複錯同一偏旁 (the same wrong radical repeated counts once) |\n\n**Teacher rule, 「繁簡混用」 (decided, Q23: feedback only).**\n- The class rule is to write in one script. Every character in the minority script is flagged with its form in the dominant script.\n- This is listed **separately from 錯別字** and **does not change the DSE estimate**, which follows HKEAA as above.\n- Evidence that HKEAA doesn't penalise mixing: Level 5 scripts include all-simplified scripts (2024 L5#3, 2025 L5#1) and mixed-script scripts (2024 L5#1, 2025 L5#3).\n\n## 3. Level descriptors (official, verbatim, [LD], marked 暫定稿 / provisional)\n\n| Level | 典型表現 |\n|---|---|\n| 5 | 緊扣主題取材；全面回應語境要求整合資料，並充分發揮。中心突出，內容豐富；用詞妥帖，文句流暢，有文采；條理分明，詳略得當，結構嚴謹。 |\n| 4 | 取材切合題意；回應大部分語境要求整合資料，並加以發揮。中心明確，內容具體；用詞準確，文句通順；條理清楚，銜接自然，詳略合宜，結構完整。 |\n| 3 | 取材切合題意；回應部分語境要求整合資料，並略加發揮。中心大致明確，意念完整；用詞正確，文句大致通順；條理清楚，詳略大致合宜，結構完整。 |\n| 2 | 取材大致切合題意；回應小部分語境要求整合資料，並稍有發揮。能表達完整意念；詞句達意；尚具篇章結構，詳略尚可。 |\n| 1 | 稍具扣題意識；粗略回應小部分語境要求。能表達零碎意念；詞句尚可達意；粗具篇章脈絡。 |\n\nThe descriptors cover both 甲部 and 乙部. The phrases about 「整合資料」 (integrating the given material) mainly apply to 甲部.\n\n## 4. Level markers for 乙部 (distilled from the exemplars)\n\nEach marker is something the scorer can observe in the text. **The most important finding:** across both years, the main thing that separates the levels is **the depth of the idea (立意) and whether the examples are analysed**. Neatness, script and length matter much less.\n\n### Level 5 (vs Level 4)\n- **The idea goes deeper than the question.** An event becomes a principle, often through a symbol or pun tied to the title.\n  - The soil is also the dirty business world, and the fake diamond becomes 本心 (2025 L5#1).\n  - 「遺忘不等於放下」 → making peace with the past (2024 L5#1).\n- **Argument essays concede a point or give counter-examples, and analyse them.**\n  - 「無愧」 is limited by 合義, with counter-examples (2024 L5#2).\n  - When giving up a promise is responsible, and when keeping one too long is not (2024 L5#3).\n  - The argument widens from the individual to society (2025 L5#3).\n- **Many examples from different eras and places, each one explained, not just named** (2024 L5#2, L5#3; 2025 L5#3).\n- **The stimulus material is reworked, not copied.** It's compressed into an insight, for example a closing 排比 (2025 L5#2).\n- **The turning point is set up earlier (伏筆) and paid off later**, not explained in a final paragraph (2025 L5#1, L5#2).\n- **Rhetoric feels natural.**\n  - 排比 「失去了童年，失去了伙伴，失去了芭比」 (2024 L5#1).\n  - A self-implicating question (2024 L5#3).\n  - The opening and ending echo through imagery, not by repeating a sentence (2025 L5#2; 2024 L5#1 「風又起，風又止」).\n- **The argument builds step by step**, for example meaning → benefit → limit → method (2024 L5#2).\n- Length is about 1,150–1,600字. **Messy handwriting and simplified or mixed scripts don't stop a script reaching Level 5.**\n\n### Level 4 (vs Level 5 / Level 3)\n- **On topic with a clear device, but the parts sit side by side instead of building.**\n  - Photos used as a thread (2024 L4#1).\n  - Four parallel scenes, each ending 「問心無愧」 (2024 L4#2).\n  - Three episodes (2025 L4#3).\n  - 首先／其次／另外 points (2024 L4#3).\n- **Reasoning is tacked on at the end:** general comments, a famous quotation, a direct appeal to the reader (2025 L4#2, L4#3).\n- **The ideas are correct but common**, for example accept yourself or change your viewpoint, without Level 5's symbolic depth (2025 L4#1).\n- **Real feeling, carried by concrete detail.** Grandpa sewing the doll (2024 L4#1). Vivid description and similes, some of them clichés (2025 L4#1, L4#2).\n- **The argument holds together and the examples fit,** including a counter-example (2024 L4#3).\n- The structure is complete and the opening and ending echo, but endings are often short or rushed (2024 L4#1, L4#3).\n- About 950–1,500字. Very neat scripts can still be Level 4, because depth is what holds them back (2024 L4#2).\n\n### Level 3 (vs Level 4 / Level 2)\n- **On topic but generic.** Examples are hypothetical or common knowledge, with no first-hand detail (2025 L3#2, L3#3). Examples are only loosely relevant (2024 L3#3).\n- **A mechanical framework.** Signposts like 從…說起／接着／然後／最後／總結來說. Examples pile up without a main point (2025 L3#2, L3#3).\n- **The position wobbles or sits on the fence.** It contradicts itself (2024 L3#2) or settles for 「兩者並無對錯」 (2024 L3#3). Some facts are wrong (2024 L3#2).\n- **Feeling comes through stock phrases:** 十分難過、悲痛欲絕、後悔莫及 (2024 L3#1). On lyrical topics, images pile up and the main idea blurs (2025 L3#1).\n- **The ending echoes the opening mechanically:** the first and last sentences are identical (2024 L3#1).\n- **Occasional strong lines but little depth.** Sentences are mostly fluent, with few figures of speech and some repeated phrases. There are more corrections than at Level 4.\n- About 950–1,250字, which overlaps Level 4, so length can't separate Level 3 from Level 4.\n\n### Level 2 (vs Level 3 / Level 1)\n- **Weak grip on the question.** The topic is read only on the surface (treasure = old belongings, 2025 L2#1), or the feeling the question asks for is thin (2024 L2#1).\n- **The argument rests on one point and one example.**\n  - Examples are only named, never analysed (2025 L2#2, L2#3; 2024 L2#3).\n  - The rebuttal is emotional rather than reasoned, and only one side of a two-sided question is handled (2024 L2#3).\n- **Narratives are a list of events in time order**, with a convenient coincidence and a direct moral at the end (2025 L2#1).\n- **Loose or unfinished structure.** The opening is unrelated to the body (2024 L2#2), or the essay is unfinished, ending on 「總括而言，」 (2025 L2#2).\n- **Sentences run on with commas.** Wording is colloquial or misused, e.g. 「大喜莫及」 (2024 L2#1).\n- Often short (about 550–800字), but not always.\n- **What separates it from Level 1:** a central idea can still be identified.\n\n### Level 1 (vs Level 2)\n- **Meaning breaks down.** The plot jumps without cause or loses track of who is who (2025 L1#1, L1#2; 2024 L1#1). There are digressions (2024 L1#2).\n- **The topic is linked by one forced sentence**, or the stimulus is listed with no development (2025 L1#2, L1#3). One vague point is repeated (2024 L1#3).\n- **Sentences get in the way of understanding:** 「我以往成任了一位合格的成年人」 (2024 L1#2). Words are misused, e.g. 「快亂的節奏」 (2025 L1#1).\n- **Punctuation breaks down**, e.g. whole paragraphs with no full stop (2024 L1#2). Wrong characters are frequent, with heavy crossings-out.\n- **Length doesn't save a script.** Scripts of about 950–1,000字 can still be Level 1 (2025 L1#1, 2024 L1#2).\n\n### Progression across levels\n- **Argument essays:** counter-examples and a concession, analysed (L5) → two sides set out side by side (L4) → a framework, but contradictory or fence-sitting (L3) → one view, one example (L2) → empty repetition (L1).\n- **Narrative and lyrical essays:** a deeper idea, with craft in the imagery and in how the opening and ending echo (L5) → real feeling and detail, but mostly telling (L4) → a complete plot told through stock phrases (L3) → a flat list of events weakly tied to the question (L2) → a jumping plot and broken sentences (L1).";

