export const ENGLISH_ERROR_TAGS = "## 5. Error tags (feedback taxonomy)\n\nThese tags drive the student's weakness profile (`error_tag_stats`). Each tag is listed with the levels where it is typical.\n\n| Tag | Example | Typical levels |\n|---|---|---|\n| `en.sva` (subject–verb agreement) | \"I fervently believes\" | L5 occasional → L3–L1 pervasive |\n| `en.verb_form` | \"we will failed\", \"was get hurt\", \"can be accept\" | all levels; it's the key L4/L3 boundary |\n| `en.tense_consistency` | tense switching in narratives | the hallmark of L4 stories; L3 and below |\n| `en.tense_choice` | \"I have joined … last month\" | L4 and below |\n| `en.passive` | \"the view will not blocked\", \"are suffered from\" | L5–L3 |\n| `en.missing_be` | \"I still scared\", \"hotel service also bad\" | L3–L1 |\n| `en.double_verb` | \"This makes social media is…\" | L3–L2 |\n| `en.article` | \"a employee\", \"a AI\" | L4–L2 |\n| `en.count_noun` | advices, feedbacks, researches, \"a staff\" | L5–L2 |\n| `en.relative_clause` | \"a student which have\" | L5–L3 |\n| `en.pronoun_case` | \"help they know\" | L2–L1 |\n| `en.preposition_pattern` | \"look forward for\", \"suggest to build\" | all levels |\n| `en.word_form` | disappointed vs disappointing, \"After pregnant\" | L4–L2 |\n| `en.word_choice` | inhibit for prohibit | all levels |\n| `en.misused_idiom` | \"strike a chord with everyone\", \"Without further ado\" at the end | L4–L2 |\n| `en.l1_transfer` | \"There have…\", \"I no friend\" | L4 and below; dominates L1 |\n| `en.run_on` | comma splices, \"and/because\" chains | L4 and below |\n| `en.fragment` | | L3–L1 |\n| `en.double_subject` | \"The manager after knowing this, he…\" | L3–L2 |\n| `en.comparative` | \"more bigger\" | L2–L1 |\n| `en.dangling_modifier` | | L5 |\n| `en.spelling` | hotal, webste | L3 and below |\n| `en.register` | contractions or threats in a formal letter | L4, L2–L1 |\n| `en.convention` | salutation and sign-off mismatch, wrong persona | L3–L1 |\n| `en.template_linkers` | memorised connectors used regardless of content | mechanical at L3–L4; pasted at L1 |\n| `en.task_copy` | prompt copied into the answer | L1 |";
